# encode_rd — matched-wall-clock encode RD harness, instrument validation
harness: scripts/encode_rd/{run_grid.py,analyze_matched.py,reproducibility.py}
         + examples/rd_tool.rs   (methodology: scripts/encode_rd/README.md)
commit: b6824e3aef45 (zenavif worktree)
date: 2026-08-08
host: Apple M4 Pro, 8 performance + 4 efficiency cores, 24 GB, macOS 26.5.2 (Darwin-25.5.0)
box_idle: NO — shared with other agents. 80 s of the 1037 s run was spent waiting
          for the free-core gate; 0 timing samples were finally dropped.

## What this run is
Instrument validation, NOT a codec result. The grid is deliberately small; the
point is to show the harness reproduces, that bytes are deterministic, and to
measure per-cell cost so the full sweep can be sized before it is launched.

## Encoder versions
zenrav1e 4d1ed620 (rav1e CLI, --features binaries)
zenav1-svt 1e0e3ef9c (rust examples/identity_run)
SVT-AV1 C reference: SVT-AV1-HDR 3115c0c (prebuilt zenav1-svt/Bin/Release/SvtAv1EncApp)
libaom: aomenc, homebrew aom 3.14.1
decoder (all arms): rav1d-safe via zenavif, 1 thread
scorer: zenmetrics 8dba5d1d, --no-default-features --features png,cpu-metrics

## Grid
images:  clic2025/training/097cb426910ba8ce2525dd8bb7fb1777.png (photo)
         gb82-sc/codec_wiki.png (screen/text)
         gb82-sc/graph.png (line-art)
sizes:   64, 256, 1024 long-edge cap (never upscaled — graph.png tops out at 796)
arms:    aom, svtc, zenrav1e, svtrs
ladder:  4, 6, 8 on each arm's own knob (cpu-used / preset / speed / preset)
rates:   8 points per arm from its own quality-spread grid (rate-stride 3)
reps:    5, interleaved and rotation-ordered, median of kept samples
config:  8-bit 4:2:0, one key frame, still-picture, 1 thread, 1 tile, CQP
cells:   864 | encodes: 4320 | 0 failed | 1037 s wall
second run (repro): same grid restricted to 256 px — 288 cells, 1440 encodes, 127 s

## Measurement definitions
time  = FULL PROCESS wall clock (spawn + init + input parse + encode + write),
        median of >=5 reps, never niced. Section C of the analysis decomposes it.
bytes = bytes_av1, the AV1 payload with the container stripped (IVF costs 44 B for
        a still; two arms write IVF and one writes a bare OBU, so file size would
        hand the OBU arm 44 free bytes — ~5% at 64x64).
score = zenmetrics ssim2 + butteraugli (max and pnorm3) + zensim, against BOTH
        ref.png (product-honest, includes the fixed 4:2:0 cost) and floor.png
        (encoder-isolated, ceiling 100). Analysis defaults to *_floor.

## Validation results
byte determinism : 864/864 cells byte-identical across all 5 repeats (4320 encodes)
byte reproducib. : 288/288 cells byte-identical across two INDEPENDENT runs
timing spread    : within-run median 1.2-3.7%, p90 5.8-9.4%; only 8/864 cells
                   exceed 20%, 7 of those at 64 px where the median is under 10 ms
timing run-to-run: geometric mean 0.988-0.997; |ln ratio| p90 0.75-2.90%,
                   max 1.57-5.80%. INSTRUMENT RESOLUTION IS ~1-3%: an A/B
                   difference smaller than that is not measurable here.
input symmetry   : 9/9 prep inputs — zenav1-svt identity_run's independent
                   BT.601 RGB->I420 is sha256-identical to rd_tool's.

## The 4:2:0 floor (encode_rd_validate_floor_2026-08-08.tsv) — read this first
ssim2 of the unencoded source round-tripped through the harness colour pair:
  photo   64/256/1024 -> 64.5 / 91.9 / 91.2
  screen  64/256/1024 -> 26.9 / 74.6 / 78.5
  lineart 64/256/796  -> 71.2 / 89.7 / 88.3
On screen content 4:2:0 chroma alone costs more than the encoder does, and at
64 px the ceiling (26.9) sits below most useful quality targets. Absolute scores
from this harness are NOT comparable to another harness's.

## Per-cell cost, and what the full sweep would cost
One cell = 5 reps. Measured s/cell (analysis section G), summed over all 4 arms
and the 3 MEASURED ladder rungs, per image per rate point:
    64 px   0.50 s      256 px   4.06 s      1024 px  40.29 s
The 1024 px tier is 89% of the cost, and zenrav1e is 78% of it (its s4 alone
costs 26.9 s/cell at 1024 — 18x its own s8).

Projected single-box wall, 3 sizes x 3 rungs x 4 arms x 5 reps:
    20 images x 20 rates ->  5.0 h
    50 images x 20 rates -> 12.5 h
    20 images x 30 rates ->  7.5 h

SCALING TO THE FULL LADDER IS NOT PROJECTED HERE. The arms have 10-14 rungs
against the 3 measured, which is x3.3-x4.7 on rung COUNT alone, and rungs 0-3
are the expensive end — extrapolating a rung cost is exactly the kind of guess
this harness exists to avoid. Bound the slow end with a probe (1 image, 2 sizes,
rungs 0-3, 3 rates, 3 reps) before committing to a full-ladder grid.
Also unmeasured: the 4096 px tier the sweep discipline asks for.

Implication: a full sweep is a fleet job, not a laptop job. Alternatively subset
the ladder per arm to the rungs that actually populate the overlap region, which
is what the matched-time reduction needs anyway.

## Files
encode_rd_validate_2026-08-08.tsv.zst  864-cell grid, one row per cell
encode_rd_repro_2026-08-08.tsv.zst     288-cell independent second run
encode_rd_validate_floor_2026-08-08.tsv  the 4:2:0 ceiling per input
encode_rd_analysis_2026-08-08.txt.zst  full analyze_matched.py output
encode_rd_repro_2026-08-08.txt         reproducibility.py output
Encoded bitstreams: content-addressed as <enc_sha256>.{ivf,obu}, 864 files /
7.5 MB, in ~/tmp/encrd/artifacts (NOT committed). Every row carries its
enc_sha256 so scalar scores can be rejoined to the exact bitstream.

## Reproduce
cd scripts/encode_rd && python3 run_grid.py \
  --images clic2025/training/097cb426910ba8ce2525dd8bb7fb1777.png,gb82-sc/codec_wiki.png,gb82-sc/graph.png \
  --sizes 64,256,1024 --arms aom,svtc,zenrav1e,svtrs \
  --ladder 4,6,8 --rate-stride 3 --reps 5 --verify-yuv --out cells.tsv
python3 analyze_matched.py cells.tsv --metric ssim2_floor --targets 30,45,60,75,88

## Known gaps
- Plane 2 (PNG -> AVIF via cavif / zenavif / avifenc) is NOT wired. payload_bytes()
  returns -1 for an ftyp file; AVIF container accounting is unimplemented.
- Ladder rungs 0-3 and 9+ are unmeasured; the slow end is where cost explodes, so
  the cost projection in analysis section G must not be extrapolated onto them.
- One image per content class. Enough to validate the instrument, nowhere near
  enough for a codec claim.
- 8-bit only. No 10-bit, no alpha, no animation, no multi-thread axis.
